================================================================================
Benchmark Datasets
================================================================================

1. DAVIS 2017 (Densely Annotated VIdeo Segmentation)
   Upstream: https://davischallenge.org/davis2017/code.html
   Citations:
     - F. Perazzi, J. Pont-Tuset, B. McWilliams, L. Van Gool, M. Gross,
       F. Sorkine-Hornung. "A Benchmark Dataset and Evaluation Methodology for
       Video Object Segmentation", CVPR 2016.
     - J. Pont-Tuset, F. Perazzi, S. Caelles, P. Arbeláez, A. Sorkine-Hornung,
       L. Van Gool. "The 2017 DAVIS Challenge on Video Object Segmentation",
       arXiv:1704.00675, 2017.
   Licence terms status:
     Annotations and benchmark video sequences are provided by the DAVIS
     organizers under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
     / CC BY-NC 4.0 terms for academic evaluation. The 30 validation sequences
     used in this study were retrieved directly from the public DAVIS repository.

2. Something-Something V2 (SSv2)
   Upstream: Twenty Billion Neurons (TwentyBN) / Qualcomm Technologies, Inc.
   URL: https://developer.qualcomm.com/software/qualcomm-neural-processing-sdk/tools/twentybn-something-something-v2
   Citation:
     - R. Goyal et al. "The 'Something Something' Video Database for Learning
       and Evaluating Visual Common Sense", ICCV 2017.
   Licence terms status:
     The SSv2 dataset was originally released by TwentyBN under academic research
     terms and is currently hosted by Qualcomm under a Research Data License
     Agreement. Commercial distribution terms could not be verified from the
     public download and require direct agreement with Qualcomm. The 200 validation
     subset clips used in this study were evaluated strictly for non-commercial
     academic benchmarking.

